    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature with minimal structural impact.\n\n**Behaviour:** `POST /api/owners` now accepts an optional `title` (e.g. `MR/MRS/MS/DR`); `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns `salutation` = `title + ' ' + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is given.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **`model/Person.java`** \u2014 added a `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) plus `getTitle()`/`setTitle()` and a small `getSalutation()`. I put these on `Person` (a tiny class) rather than the large `Owner` class to keep the surrounding-complexity cost (`WMC_other`) low. MapStruct auto-maps `title` (in) and `salutation` (out) by property name \u2014 exactly like the existing `initials` field \u2014 so **`OwnerMapper` needed no change**.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` to the `OwnerFields` request schema and a read-only `salutation` to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated DTOs carry both.\n- **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added a `title VARCHAR(10)` column (appended at the end of the `owners` table). This is the authoritative schema for the test profile (`ddl-auto=none`); the h2/postgres/mysql schemas are minimal starter tables relying on `ddl-auto=update` and already omit most columns, so I left them consistent with that convention.\n- **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a `NULL` to each seed `owners` insert to match the new positional column.\n\nNo `@RestController`/`@Mapping` edits were needed, and no function bodies in large classes were touched.",
